# Crystal H(T) at ONE temperature under the target potential -> ht.dat.
#
# GibbsCurveMaker runs one of these per ladder temperature; with
# G0 = F_TI + dG_switch at T0, the sweep is integrated by Gibbs-Helmholtz,
# G(T) = T [G0/T0 - int_T0^T H/T'^2 dT'], so Cp(T) is the MD's own.
#
# The `tri` barostat lets a low-symmetry cell change SHAPE, not just volume;
# forcing it orthogonal leaves residual shear stress that stiffens exactly
# the phonons this run measures. The short NVT leg equilibrates the velocity
# distribution BEFORE the barostat sees the cell.
#
# Outputs: ht.dat (measured T, enthalpy, volume), final.data.

units metal
atom_style atomic
boundary p p p
read_data input.data
${maybe_triclinic}

pair_style ${pair_style}
pair_coeff * * ${potential_path} ${species_string}

timestep ${time_step}
thermo ${thermo_interval}
thermo_style custom step temp pe press vol enthalpy
thermo_modify flush yes
variable tt equal temp
variable hh equal enthalpy
variable vv equal vol

velocity all create ${temperature} ${seed} mom yes rot yes
fix th all nvt temp ${temperature} ${temperature} 0.1
run 2000
unfix th

fix p all npt temp ${temperature} ${temperature} 0.1 ${barostat} 0.0 0.0 2.0
fix av all ave/time 10 50 500 v_tt v_hh v_vv file ht.dat
run ${n_run}
unfix av
unfix p
write_data final.data
